    "text": "The temperature of equal masses of three different liquids <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> respectively. The temperature of mixture when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is mixed with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and that when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math> is mixed with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>26</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The temperature of mixture when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> are mixed will be :"
